<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolt</p><h1 class="enc-title">Second Serbian Uprising</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1815">1815</a>–<a href="/years/1817">1817</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Second Serbian Uprising was a revolt of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbs">Serbs</a> against Ottoman rule, launched at Takovo in April 1815 under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milos-obrenovic">Miloš Obrenović</a>. Combining fighting with negotiation, Miloš won a measure of self-government from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a>, and the autonomous Principality of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbia">Serbia</a> that emerged was formally recognised by the sultan in 1830.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/second-serbian-uprising.jpg" alt="Second Serbian Uprising" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Muzej rudničko-takovskog kraja u Gornjem Milanovcu · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Paja_Jovanovi%C4%87,_Takovski_ustanak.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
